Two four-band elementary band representations, and whether their bands can
be separated: SG 199 (Flicker et al., PRB 98, 155145) and SG 208 (Cano et
al., PRL 120, 266401).

1. SG 199: the group, and the levels of the four bands
   realized group   : #199.13 I2_131', s orbitals at Wyckoff 8a, 4 bands
   GM : GM4(3) @ -1.000000, GM1(1) @ +3.000000
   H  : H1(1) @ -3.000000, H4(3) @ +1.000000
   N  : N1(1) @ -2.236068, N2(1) @ -1.000000, N2(1) @ +1.000000, N1(1) @ +2.236068
   P  : P1(2) @ -1.732051, P3(2) @ +1.732051
   PA : PA1(2) @ -1.732051, PA3(2) @ +1.732051
   GM4 and H4 are threefold: the spin-1 fermions

2. SG 199: the four bands together, and the three inter-band gaps
   all four bands   : GM1 + GM4 + H1 + H4 + 2×N1 + 2×N2 + P1 + P3 + PA1 + PA3
                      = 1 x A1↑G(4)@8a(31',3)
   min over a 13^3 mesh of E1-E0 / E2-E1 / E3-E2:
                      0.000000 / 0.000000 / 0.000000
   every inter-band gap closes somewhere, so no subset of the four bands is
   isolated at any filling: this elementary band representation is connected

3. SG 208: the group, the crystal field the paper draws, and the levels
   realized group   : #208.45 P4_2321', orbitals at Wyckoff 2a, 4 bands
                      (the 24 atoms of the crystal field are the paper's own
                      device, and carry no orbital)
   GM : GM3(2) @ -0.861626, GM3(2) @ +0.861626
   M  : M5(2) @ -0.258199, M5(2) @ +0.258199
   R  : R3(2) @ -1.200000, R3(2) @ +1.200000
   X  : X5(2) @ -0.258199, X5(2) @ +0.258199

4. SG 208: the four bands together, and the three inter-band gaps
   all four bands   : 2×GM3 + 2×M5 + 2×R3 + 2×X5
                      = 1 x 1E2E↑G(4)@2a(231',23)
   min over a 13^3 mesh of E1-E0 / E2-E1 / E3-E2:
                      0.000000 / 0.256971 / 0.000000
   indirect gap at half filling: 0.256971
   the middle gap never closes, so this elementary band representation is
   split at half filling: two isolated halves of two bands each

5. SG 208: each half of the split, asked on its own
   bands 0, 1       : GM3 + M5 + R3 + X5   decompose: none
   bands 2, 3       : GM3 + M5 + R3 + X5   decompose: none
   no sum of elementary band representations has either content, so each
   isolated half is topological

6. the bands of both models, one panel each

